# Commits listed here are ignored by `git blame` (and GitHub's blame view,
# which reads this file automatically). Use it for commits that are pure
# reformatting/rename and change no logic, so blame keeps pointing at the
# commit that actually changed behavior.
#
# Configure git to use this locally:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Add an entry whenever you land a formatting-only commit (e.g. running
# `.clang-format` over a module for the first time, per ROADMAP.md's
# "`.clang-format` rollout to existing files" item). One hash per line,
# full 40-character SHA, with a short comment above it.
 
# Example (remove once a real formatting commit lands):
# 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
 
